---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
import AdSlot from '@components/AdSlot.astro';
---

<Layout
  lang="en"
  title="Palworld Breeding Guide - 287x287 Complete Combos"
  description="Palworld breeding complete guide. Full 287x287 matrix, exclusive recipes, shortest path. Find any child Pal from any parent pair in seconds."
>
  <article class="guide-content">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/en/guides/">Guides</a> › Breeding Guide</p>
      <h1>🧬 Palworld Breeding Guide: 287×287 Complete Combos</h1>
      <p class="text-secondary">40,972 breeding edges · Palworld 1.0 + Sakurajima + Feybreak</p>
    </header>

    <AdSlot position="inline" />

    <section>
      <h2>How Breeding Works: Parents Determine the Child</h2>
      <p>
        Palworld breeding is based on <strong>parent pairs</strong>. Each pair of parents (gender-independent)
        produces 1-2 fixed children. The child's rarity follows a probability distribution:
        normal 60% / Alpha 35% / Lucky 5%.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Child = lookup result of parent pair</strong>, not random</li>
        <li><strong>Stronger parents tend to produce stronger children</strong> - <a href="/en/pals/jormuntide">Jormuntide</a> + any dragon parent often produces a dragon boss</li>
        <li><strong>Breeding passes skills, not stats</strong> - child stats = child species baseline</li>
        <li>There is an <strong>inbreeding penalty</strong> - too-close bloodlines reduce rarity</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Wondering what two Pals produce? Try our <a href="/en/breeding/">Breeding Calculator</a> -
        it supports forward queries (parent + parent → child), reverse queries (I want X, give me parents),
        and shortest-path queries (minimum steps to breed a target from what you already have).
      </p>
    </section>

    <AdSlot position="inline" />

    <section>
      <h2>Early-Game Must-Know: 5 Exclusive Recipes</h2>
      <p>These combos work as soon as you unlock the <a href="/en/tech-tree/monsterfarm">Ranch</a> at level 5:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Pengullet + Cattiva</strong> = <a href="/en/pals/petallia">Petallia</a> - dual-purpose grass/harvest Pal</li>
        <li><strong>Lifmunk + Cattiva</strong> = <a href="/en/pals/mozzarina">Mozzarina</a> - milk production, used in every recipe</li>
        <li><strong>Jolthog + Pengullet</strong> = early electric Pal, useful for power generation</li>
        <li><strong>Pengullet + Foxparks</strong> = fast water-typing breeding base</li>
        <li><strong>Cattiva + Lifmunk</strong> = <a href="/en/pals/helzephyr">Helzephyr</a> (event variant) - top mid-game flying Pal</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <AdSlot position="inline" />

    <section>
      <h2>Mid-Game Boss Recipes: 5 High-Value Combos</h2>
      <p>After you reach level 20+ and unlock advanced tech, these boss-level combos are worth breeding:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Anubis + Blazamut</strong> = <a href="/en/pals/faleris">Faleris</a> - flying + fire + mount, triple utility</li>
        <li><strong>Bushi + Anubis</strong> = <a href="/en/pals/orpalka">Orpalka</a> - water-dragon boss, crushes 60+ content</li>
        <li><strong>Frostallion + Foxparks Cryst</strong> = <a href="/en/pals/frostallion-noct">Frostallion Noct</a> - dark-ice boss pre-evolution</li>
        <li><strong>Rayhound + Jormuntide</strong> = <a href="/en/pals/grizzbolt">Grizzbolt</a> - electric core boss</li>
        <li><strong>Anubis + Silveon</strong> = <a href="/en/pals/silveon">Silveon</a> (shiny) - dark-type damage king</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <AdSlot position="inline" />

    <section>
      <h2>Feybreak DLC: New Breeding Combos</h2>
      <p>Feybreak DLC (January 2026) added 12 new Pals with completely independent breeding trees:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Xenovader + any dragon</strong> = chance of <a href="/en/pals/xenolord">Xenolord</a> (dark-dragon boss)</li>
        <li><strong>Hartalis + any ground</strong> = chance of <a href="/en/pals/solmora">Solmora</a> (new ground-type Pal)</li>
        <li><strong>Bellanoir Libero</strong> self-breed = 100% shiny <a href="/en/pals/bellanoir">Bellanoir</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <AdSlot position="inline" />

    <section>
      <h2>Pro Tips: How to Get Target Pals Fast</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Use the shortest-path query</strong> - want Jormuntide but no dragon parents? The calculator finds combos from Pals you already own</li>
        <li><strong>One pair per Ranch</strong> - splitting up Pals across multiple Ranches is fastest</li>
        <li><strong>Shiny rate depends on parent breedPower</strong> - higher breedPower parents = higher shiny odds</li>
        <li><strong>Don't use egg incubators</strong> with time boosts - they reduce rarity probability</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="related-links">
      <h2>Use Right Now</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/en/breeding/">🧮 Breeding Calculator (4 query modes)</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/pals/">📖 Paldex (288 Pals)</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/guides/boss-guide/">⚔️ Boss Strategies</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/guides/tech-tree-guide/">🔬 Tech Tree</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .guide-content { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; line-height: 1.8; }
  .page-header { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .breadcrumb { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  h1 { font-size: 2rem; margin: 0.5rem 0; line-height: 1.3; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem; color: var(--accent); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); padding-left: 0.8rem; }
  p { margin: 0.8rem 0; }
  ul, ol { margin: 0.8rem 0; padding-left: 1.5rem; }
  li { margin: 0.5rem 0; }
  a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; }
  .related-links { margin-top: 3rem; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--bg-secondary); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); }
  .related-links ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .related-links li { padding: 0.3rem 0; }
</style>
